# HopHacks ink pipeline

Draw on an Android phone over the LAN; the laptop stores each drawing and runs
analysis on it. Partly an accessibility tool for stroke patients with tremor and
limited finger mobility. `readME.md` explains how it works; this file is the
state and the working agreements.

## Working agreements

- **Confirm before building anything new.** Explain the plan and wait for a go.
- **Reminder to push** goes at the end of any list of commands, nowhere else.
- Always invoke Python as `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe`. A bare `python` grabs
  the system interpreter, which lacks the dependencies and has already caused a
  second server to seize port 8000 while the venv one bound to nothing.
- Verify with the scripts in `scripts/` before claiming something works.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `run.py` | Launcher: LAN address, QR code, firewall check |
| `server/config.py` | Settings from env and `.env`, smoothing presets |
| `server/storage.py` | Disk writes, `index.jsonl`, `answers.jsonl`, DB seam |
| `server/app.py` | Routes, WebSocket hub, `ask_tablet()`, `analyse()` |
| `server/pipeline.py` | Step 2 hook, currently returns `SAMPLE_TEXT` |
| `server/speech.py` | ElevenLabs synthesis, `data/tts/` cache, never raises |
| `web/canvas.html/js` | Tablet surface: drawing, idle capture, taps, speech |
| `web/viewer.html/js` | Optional desktop view, purely a listener |

Tests, each starting its own server on a free port: `browser_test.py` (capture
loop), `tap_test.py` (tap answers, multi-touch), `smoothing_test.py` (tremor
filter), `pipeline_test.py` (what step 2 receives), `speech_test.py` (synthesis,
caching, keyless fallback, confirming tap). Also `smoke_test.py`, `ask.py`,
`show_data.py`, `show_strokes.py` against a running server.

## Status

**Step 1 is complete and tested.** Capture after 20s of inactivity, PNG plus
stroke JSON plus `index.jsonl`, optional viewer, tap-to-answer (one tap yes, two
no), stroke start/end tones and vibration, One Euro tremor smoothing.

**Only the API call itself is left in step 2.** `pipeline.process_capture(image,
data)` prints a summary and returns `SAMPLE_TEXT`; the user replaces its body
with the real call. `image` is a `Path`; `data` is `{"points": [[x, y], ...]
flattened across all strokes in drawing order, "strokes": count}`. Called from
`analyse()` after the upload response, on a worker thread.

**Speech and confirmation are built and tested.** `analyse()` hands the text to
`speech.synthesise()`, pushes `{"type": "speak", "text", "url"}` to tablets, then
`ask_tablet("Did I get that right?")`, whose tap lands in `answers.jsonl` with
the capture id and text in `context`. No API key yet: the user will add
`ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` to `.env`, and until then the tablet speaks with its own
`speechSynthesis`. Model still undecided — `eleven_flash_v2_5` by default,
switchable to `eleven_multilingual_v2` if hackathon credits come through.

**Tiger Data is parked** until everything else is done. Nothing is wired; only
an unused `INK_DATABASE_URL` and an empty `CaptureStore.sinks`.

**No getter function exists.** Reading data back means `CaptureStore.recent()`,
the HTTP routes, or the scripts. The user intends to specify one.

## Gotchas worth remembering

- Bump `CLIENT_VERSION` in **both** `web/canvas.js` and `server/app.py` on any
  frontend change. A tablet's socket silently reconnects after a server
  restart, so a stale page looks healthy while running old code; the version
  check forces a reload. This has already cost an hour of debugging.
- The key `strokes` is a list of stroke dicts inside a capture's `.json`, but a
  filename string inside `index.jsonl`. Same name, different type.
- Stroke points are `[x, y, pressure, t]` in **CSS pixels**; the PNG is `dpr`
  times larger. `t` is a shared clock across all strokes in one capture.
- Pressure is always 0.5 and `tool` is always `touch`: finger, not stylus.
- Smoothed strokes keep a `raw` array of unfiltered points. Never drop it; the
  tremor is potentially the clinically interesting signal.
- Tremor smoothing needs a far smaller One Euro `beta` than the usual examples,
  because tremor is fast and a large beta raises the cutoff during the shake.
  Filter each axis with its own speed, not a shared one.
- No sound or vibration on the first stroke after a page load, by browser
  policy. The user has decided to live with it; do not "fix" it unprompted.
- iPadOS has no `navigator.vibrate`. Android is the only target.
- Speech must never be able to fail loudly. `synthesise()` returns None instead
  of raising, and a null `url` tells the tablet to speak the text itself.
- The free ElevenLabs tier requires the "Powered by ElevenLabs" line, which the
  canvas shows only when their audio actually played.
- `ELEVENLABS_BASE_URL` exists so `speech_test.py` can point synthesis at a stub.
  Nothing else should need it.
- Redirecting a server's stdout to a file buffers it; use `python -u` when
  capturing output for inspection.
